{"name": "dsagent.note", "value": {"run_id": "run-eda-003", "step": "data-gate", "persona": "marie", "text": "I evaluated all four applicable gate thresholds from the `eda` skill against `artifacts/data-profile.json` (no reloading/recomputation of the dataset):\n\n- **Null share** (all 6 columns): 0.0 %, threshold >20 % \u2014 PASS\n- **Exact duplicate rows**: 0.0 %, threshold >1 % \u2014 PASS\n- **Key uniqueness** (`date`): `unique: true`, 0 duplicates \u2014 PASS\n- **Missing time periods**: 1,461 expected vs. 1,461 observed daily periods (2012-01-01 to 2015-12-31), 0 missing \u2014 PASS\n\nWrote `artifacts/data-gate.md` with one row per check (value / threshold / denominator), a **Flags** section for non-blocking issues to carry forward as caveats, and the final line `GATE: PASS`.\n\nFlags for the next (analysis) step to carry as caveats:\n- `precipitation` is heavily right-skewed (14.1 % beyond IQR fence) \u2014 prefer median/log scale over raw means.\n- `wind` has a smaller outlier tail (2.3 %).\n- `weather` category mix drifts noticeably by year (e.g., snow and drizzle both decline sharply 2012\u21922015), possibly a classification artifact rather than a real trend.\n- No station/location metadata \u2014 findings should be scoped to this one record, not \"Seattle\" broadly.\n- `weather` is a single label per day, so mixed conditions are undercounted.\n- Row-level `temp_max \u2265 temp_min` consistency wasn't checked in the profile and should be verified before temperature-range analysis.\n\nNo concerns block progress \u2014 the gate passed cleanly and the dataset is small and complete, so the next step can proceed straight to analysis.", "ts": 1789610595.5369332}}
