{"name": "dsagent.note", "value": {"run_id": "run-eda-003", "step": "analyze", "persona": "noel", "text": "All four figures and `artifacts/findings.md` are in place. Summary:\n\n**What I did:**\n- Read the data profile and gate report \u2014 dataset passes the gate (1,461 daily rows, 2012\u20132015, no nulls/dupes/missing days), with flagged caveats on precipitation skew and year-over-year drift in `weather` category mix.\n- Loaded `data/seattle-weather.csv` and computed:\n  - Category-level precipitation and temperature stats (median/IQR for precip given its skew; mean \u00b1 95% CI for temperature).\n  - A season-adjusted trend model (daily OLS with year + sine/cosine day-of-year terms, HC3 robust SEs, n=1,461) to test direction over time for `temp_max`, `temp_min`, and `precipitation`, per the \"must fit a trend, not assert one\" rule.\n- Produced 4 figures under `artifacts/figures/` (colorblind-safe palette, single axis each, message-bearing titles): precipitation by category, temperature by category, temperature trend 2012\u20132015, precipitation trend 2012\u20132015.\n- Wrote `artifacts/findings.md` with exactly the three required sections (Headline findings / Evidence / Caveats), each headline number carrying its denominator and, for the trend claim, slope + 95% CI.\n\n**Key results:** `rain`/`snow` carry essentially all measured precipitation while `sun`/`fog`/`drizzle` are near-zero; temperature cleanly separates categories (`snow` coldest, `sun` warmest, ~14 \u00b0C gap, non-overlapping CIs); both temperature extremes rose significantly 2012\u21922015 (+0.73 \u00b0C/yr max, +0.51 \u00b0C/yr min, CIs exclude zero) while precipitation showed no clear trend (CI straddles zero).\n\n**Concerns for the report step:** the `weather` category mix itself drifts year over year (e.g., snow 21\u21922 days, drizzle 31\u21927) in a way that could be observer/instrument classification drift rather than real climate change \u2014 I treated this as a caveat, not a headline finding, and left it for the report step to decide whether it belongs under \"what the data cannot answer.\" I did not attempt any causal or predictive claims, per scope.", "ts": 1789610879.3634539}}
