{"name": "dsagent.note", "value": {"run_id": "run-eda-003", "step": "report", "persona": "marie", "text": "All checks pass: the three headline findings are present verbatim, and all 4 figures are embedded as base64 images. The HTML file is non-empty (272 KB).\n\nSummary of what I did:\n- Read the `reports` skill and the three input artifacts (`findings.md`, `data-profile.md`, `data-gate.md`). The gate verdict is **PASS** with no threshold breaches, so I carried the three headline findings from `findings.md` forward unchanged \u2014 they don't contradict the gate.\n- Wrote `report/findings.md` following the required structure: 3 headline findings, context (question/data/grain/row count), a **\"What this data cannot answer\"** section built from the gate's flags and the profile's coverage notes (no station metadata, daily-only grain, single-label weather category, category-mix drift, and the limits of a 4-year trend), an evidence section per finding referencing all four figures, a data-quality-notes section mirroring the gate's non-blocking flags, a **\"Next steps\"** section I authored (row-consistency check, station metadata, trend robustness over more years, log/zero-inflated precipitation modeling, sub-daily data), and an appendix with the full numeric tables.\n- Rendered it to `report/findings.html` via the skill's `render_html.py`, using image paths relative to `report/` (`../artifacts/figures/...`) since the renderer resolves images relative to the markdown file's directory.\n- Verified the HTML exists, is non-trivial in size, contains all three headline finding sentences, and has all 4 figures embedded as base64 data URIs.\n\nConcerns for the next step: the report explicitly flags that `weather`-category drift over the years looks like classification/instrument change rather than climate signal, and that `temp_max \u2265 temp_min` row-level consistency was never verified \u2014 both should be resolved before any deeper modeling builds on this dataset.", "ts": 1789610935.8913002}}
